From: WadOS <wados@wadspaces.com>
Subject: [PATCH] layer-shell: a client turning on-demand on gets the keys

A layer surface that's mapped and changes its keyboard interactivity to
on-demand (from none) is given keyboard focus, unless an exclusive layer
has it. Stock labwc only gives on-demand surfaces focus on a click (and,
for top and overlay, when they map), so a bottom-layer desktop couldn't
take the keys without one.

WadOS's shell uses it when its desktop page comes into view by the keys
(Page Down, ↓ from the launcher): the desktop's keys work at once. Only
the host's own clients have layer-shell (sandboxed clients don't see it).
---
 src/layers.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/layers.c b/src/layers.c
index 60421e3..ff956e2 100644
--- a/src/layers.c
+++ b/src/layers.c
@@ -286,6 +286,13 @@ handle_surface_commit(struct wl_listener *listener, void *data)
 				 */
 				struct server *server = layer->server;
 				try_to_focus_next_layer_or_toplevel(server);
+			} else if (layer_surface->surface->mapped) {
+				/*
+				 * A mapped client turning on-demand on (from
+				 * none) asks for the keys: give them, unless an
+				 * exclusive layer has them.
+				 */
+				layer_try_set_focus(seat, layer_surface);
 			}
 			goto out;
 		}
